WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.350
Zoom in on the inner lining
of your small intestine,

2
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.350
one cell at a time.

3
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:11.510
Each cell facing the gut wears a fringe of
tiny finger-like folds called microvilli.

4
00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:14.530
Thousands of them, packed side by side.

5
00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:18.370
Why would a cell bother to
grow so many tiny folds?

6
00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:22.140
In this mission, you'll find out
what sets the speed of diffusion,

7
00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:25.300
and combine those factors
in one calculation.

8
00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:29.260
Then you'll read data on two
substances entering cells:

9
00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:32.690
one rises steadily, the other levels off.

10
00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:37.220
Your mission: explain why the cells
lining the small intestine are covered in

11
00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:38.430
tiny folds.
